# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-accuracy quantum chemistry on reduced systems,\n"
msgstr "Chimie quantique de haute précision sur des systèmes réduits,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-checking ZNE or other mitigation methods.\n"
msgstr "Vérification croisée de ZNE ou d'autres méthodes de mitigation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC's relationship to other mitigation methods {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"
msgstr "Relation de PEC avec les autres méthodes de mitigation {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many other mitigation techniques trade accuracy for scalability; PEC does just the opposite, focusing on accuracy above all else.\n"
msgstr "De nombreuses autres techniques de mitigation sacrifient la précision au profit de la scalabilité ; PEC fait exactement le contraire, en privilégiant la précision avant tout.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because PEC might only be used on a subcircuit, it is especially important here to ask what other mitigation methods can be combined with it. To reason clearly about compatibility with PEC, it helps to categorize techniques by what they do to the noise. Consider these general categories:\n"
msgstr "Comme PEC peut n'être utilisée que sur un sous-circuit, il est particulièrement important de se demander quelles autres méthodes de mitigation peuvent lui être combinées. Pour raisonner clairement sur la compatibilité avec PEC, il est utile de classer les techniques selon ce qu'elles font au bruit. Considère ces catégories générales :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise cancellation - attempt to invert error channels\n"
msgstr "Annulation du bruit : tentative d'inverser les canaux d'erreur\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise scaling - deliberately increase noise to extrapolate\n"
msgstr "Mise à l'échelle du bruit : augmentation délibérée du bruit pour extrapoler\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise reshaping - change the structure or spectrum of noise\n"
msgstr "Remodelage du bruit : modification de la structure ou du spectre du bruit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bias removal - correct errors that do not scale with gate noise\n"
msgstr "Suppression du biais : correction des erreurs qui ne varient pas avec le bruit des Gates\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC sits squarely in category (1). Any method that changes or rescales the noise channel must be examined carefully.\n"
msgstr "PEC se situe clairement dans la catégorie (1). Toute méthode qui modifie ou remet à l'échelle le canal de bruit doit être examinée avec soin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary table (high-level)\n"
msgstr "Tableau récapitulatif (vue d'ensemble)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Technique | Compatible with PEC | Notes |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | No | Undoing versus scaling and sometimes tailoring error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Yes (with care) | Affects error behavior, but might make it easier to learn |\n"
"| TREX | Yes | No overlap in workflow. Fully compatible. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Usually no | Changes error channel |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Technique | Compatible avec PEC | Remarques |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | Non | Annuler contre mettre à l'échelle, et parfois adapter l'erreur |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Oui (avec précaution) | Affecte le comportement de l'erreur, mais peut faciliter son apprentissage |\n"
"| TREX | Oui | Aucun chevauchement dans le workflow. Entièrement compatible. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Généralement non | Modifie le canal d'erreur |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and ZNE address the same error sources (gate errors) via mutually incompatible assumptions or workstreams, or both. For example, in ZNE, we assume error can be expanded in a parameter $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"and that the error can be effectively scaled to model this expansion. PEC would undo the very error we rely on for the scaling. The parameter $\\lambda$ would become meaningless. Another way of thinking about it is:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC et ZNE traitent les mêmes sources d'erreur (erreurs de Gates) avec des hypothèses ou des flux de travail mutuellement incompatibles, ou les deux. Par exemple, dans ZNE, on suppose que l'erreur peut être développée en fonction d'un paramètre $\\lambda$ :\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"et que l'erreur peut être effectivement mise à l'échelle pour modéliser ce développement. PEC annulerait justement l'erreur sur laquelle repose la mise à l'échelle. Le paramètre $\\lambda$ perdrait tout sens. Une autre façon de voir les choses :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying ZNE before PEC changes the noise channel you are trying to invert.\n"
msgstr "Appliquer ZNE avant PEC modifie le canal de bruit que tu essaies d'inverser.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC before ZNE removes the very noise ZNE relies on to extrapolate.\n"
msgstr "Appliquer PEC avant ZNE supprime le bruit même sur lequel ZNE s'appuie pour extrapoler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC and ZNE should be considered alternative error-mitigation paradigms, not composable layers. Comparing them side-by-side is instructive, while combining them is not.\n"
msgstr "PEC et ZNE doivent être considérées comme des paradigmes de mitigation d'erreur alternatifs, et non comme des couches composables. Les comparer côte à côte est instructif, alors que les combiner ne l'est pas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and Pauli twirling are generally compatible and often beneficial.\n"
"Twirling might help PEC in that twirling converts coherent errors into stochastic Pauli errors. This simplifies the noise channel, making it easier to represent and invert. For PEC, this is extremely valuable, for the following reasons:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC et Pauli twirling sont généralement compatibles et souvent bénéfiques.\n"
"Le twirling peut aider PEC dans la mesure où il convertit les erreurs cohérentes en erreurs de Pauli stochastiques. Cela simplifie le canal de bruit, ce qui le rend plus facile à représenter et à inverser. Pour PEC, c'est extrêmement précieux, pour les raisons suivantes :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decompositions are much simpler for Pauli channels\n"
msgstr "Les décompositions en quasi-probabilités sont beaucoup plus simples pour les canaux de Pauli\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quasi-probability norm $\\gamma$ is often significantly smaller\n"
msgstr "La norme de quasi-probabilité $\\gamma$ est souvent nettement plus petite\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling variance is reduced\n"
msgstr "La variance d'échantillonnage est réduite\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Many PEC demonstrations assume or build in Pauli-twirled noise.\n"
"It's important to clarify that Pauli twirling does not mitigate errors by itself; it reshapes noise into a form that probabilistic error cancellation can handle more efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"De nombreuses démonstrations de PEC supposent ou intègrent un bruit soumis au Pauli twirling.\n"
"Il est important de préciser que le Pauli twirling ne mitige pas les erreurs à lui seul ; il remodèle le bruit sous une forme que l'annulation probabiliste d'erreurs peut traiter plus efficacement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC can and should be combined with TREX. These approaches are fully compatible and play orthogonal roles. TREX operates only at measurement, removes readout bias via randomized twirls of the measurement channel, and does not affect gate noise or circuit dynamics. PEC operates on gate noise. Because measurement error is additive rather than compositional, it is independent of gate sequences. It is safe and often desirable to apply TREX alongside PEC.\n"
msgstr "PEC peut et doit être combinée avec TREX. Ces approches sont entièrement compatibles et jouent des rôles orthogonaux. TREX n'agit qu'à la mesure, supprime le biais de lecture via des twirls aléatoires du canal de mesure, et n'affecte ni le bruit des Gates ni la dynamique du Circuit. PEC agit sur le bruit des Gates. Comme l'erreur de mesure est additive plutôt que compositionnelle, elle est indépendante des séquences de Gates. Il est sûr, et souvent souhaitable, d'appliquer TREX en parallèle de PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ordering of these methods is what you might expect:\n"
"1. Execute PEC-randomized circuit\n"
"2. Apply TREX to mitigate readout error\n"
"3. Apply PEC weighting and averaging\n"
msgstr ""
"L'ordre de ces méthodes est celui auquel tu pourrais t'attendre :\n"
"1. Exécuter le Circuit randomisé de PEC\n"
"2. Appliquer TREX pour mitiger l'erreur de lecture\n"
"3. Appliquer la pondération et la moyenne de PEC\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and DD are generally incompatible unless the noise characterization used for PEC is performed with DD active. PEC assumes that $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"is stationary, repeatable, and accurately characterizable. DD explicitly reshapes the noise channel in time by modulating system-environment interactions and introducing non-trivial pulse-timing effects. As a result, the effective noise with DD is not the same channel as without DD. This is made even more complex by the fact that the noise channel can depend sensitively on circuit scheduling. The end result is that noise inversion becomes ill-defined or invalid.\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC et DD sont généralement incompatibles, sauf si la caractérisation du bruit utilisée pour PEC est effectuée avec DD actif. PEC suppose que $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"est stationnaire, reproductible et caractérisable avec précision. DD remodèle explicitement le canal de bruit dans le temps en modulant les interactions système-environnement et en introduisant des effets de minutage d'impulsions non triviaux. En conséquence, le bruit effectif avec DD n'est pas le même canal que sans DD. Cela est encore compliqué par le fait que le canal de bruit peut dépendre fortement de l'ordonnancement du Circuit. Au final, l'inversion du bruit devient mal définie ou invalide.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is theoretically possible to characterize noise with DD active and build a PEC model accordingly, but this is highly advanced and not currently a recommended workflow.\n"
msgstr "Il est théoriquement possible de caractériser le bruit avec DD actif et de construire un modèle PEC en conséquence, mais c'est très avancé et ce n'est pas actuellement un workflow recommandé.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC by hand {#applying-pec-by-hand}"
msgstr "Appliquer PEC à la main {#applying-pec-by-hand}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is complex and it is not recommended that you implement it by hand. Still, we want to work through the math of a basic application on a single qubit to understand what steps the process entails. We choose a mixed but nontrivial state so that we can see numerical effects clearly.\n"
msgstr "PEC est complexe et il n'est pas recommandé de l'implémenter à la main. Néanmoins, nous voulons dérouler les calculs d'une application de base sur un seul Qubit pour comprendre les étapes du processus. Nous choisissons un état mixte mais non trivial afin de bien voir les effets numériques.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Take a qubit that should be in the pure state\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Prenons un Qubit qui devrait se trouver dans l'état pur\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ideal density matrix is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"La matrice densité idéale est :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"We've chosen this density matrix because it is not diagonal and is only for a single qubit so that it is tractable to examine \"by hand\".\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Nous avons choisi cette matrice densité parce qu'elle n'est pas diagonale et ne concerne qu'un seul Qubit, ce qui permet de l'examiner « à la main ».\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now apply a very simple, but realistic noise model: a single-qubit depolarizing channel, with small strength $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous appliquons maintenant un modèle de bruit très simple mais réaliste : un canal dépolarisant à un Qubit, de faible intensité $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep the arithmetic friendly, take $p = 0.15$. This channel is completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP), as it must be. It is a realistic noise channel for real hardware, or at least realistic for describing some of the noise. Further, this noise channel is analytically invertible, as a linear map. In other words, there exists an inverse matrix, but that doesn't mean that the matrix corresponds to a CPTP physical channel, and it certainly doesn't correspond to a unitary that could be implemented on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Pour simplifier les calculs, prenons $p = 0.15$. Ce canal est complètement positif et préserve la trace (CPTP), comme il se doit. C'est un canal de bruit réaliste pour du matériel réel, ou du moins pour décrire une partie du bruit. De plus, ce canal de bruit est analytiquement inversible, en tant qu'application linéaire. En d'autres termes, il existe une matrice inverse, mais cela ne signifie pas que cette matrice correspond à un canal physique CPTP, et elle ne correspond certainement pas à une unitaire qui pourrait être implémentée sur du matériel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we apply our depolarizing noise channel to our single-qubit density matrix and obtain:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"With $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ and $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Appliquons maintenant notre canal de bruit dépolarisant à notre matrice densité à un Qubit, ce qui donne :\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"Avec $p = 0.15$ : $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ et $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying this to our state:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"En l'appliquant à notre état :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute explicitly:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Calculons explicitement :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(rounded)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"This is still a physical density matrix, and it still has trace one &mdash; but it is more mixed now.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(arrondi)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"C'est toujours une matrice densité physique, et sa trace vaut toujours un &mdash; mais elle est désormais plus mélangée.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we compute the ideal inverse channel, but being very prepared for the possibility that it might not be physical. We will check whether it is. Mathematically, the inverse linear map is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Calculons maintenant le canal inverse idéal, en étant bien préparés à la possibilité qu'il ne soit pas physique. Nous vérifierons si c'est le cas. Mathématiquement, l'application linéaire inverse est :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If this inverse action were itself a valid physical channel, then we would be tempted to try to implement it exactly. Of course, we would still need to figure out how to implement it using unitary operations and classical steps, but implementing this would be the goal. However, it turns out this is *not* CPTP, and there is generally no guarantee that such inverse mappings will be CPTP. That is critical to our current discussion, because it is the reason PEC exists.\n"
msgstr "Si cette action inverse était elle-même un canal physique valide, nous serions tentés de l'implémenter exactement. Bien sûr, il faudrait encore trouver comment l'implémenter à l'aide d'opérations unitaires et d'étapes classiques, mais ce serait l'objectif. Cependant, il s'avère qu'elle n'est *pas* CPTP, et rien ne garantit en général que de telles applications inverses soient CPTP. C'est essentiel pour notre discussion, car c'est la raison d'être de PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might be able to see that it is not CPTP just by looking at it. A sure-fire check is to apply it to a density matrix and see if it returns physical results. This is left as an exercise to check your understanding.\n"
msgstr "Tu peux peut-être voir qu'elle n'est pas CPTP rien qu'en la regardant. Une vérification infaillible consiste à l'appliquer à une matrice densité et à voir si elle renvoie des résultats physiques. Nous laissons cela en exercice pour vérifier ta compréhension.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Vérifie ta compréhension {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether the inverse mapping from above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ is CPTP by applying it to a new density matrix:\n"
msgstr "Vérifie si l'application inverse $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ ci-dessus est CPTP en l'appliquant à une nouvelle matrice densité :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpret the results as being physical or non-physical.\n"
msgstr "Interprète les résultats comme physiques ou non physiques.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a physical density matrix, this corresponds to a classical probability of greater than 1 that the system is in the state $|0\\rangle$ and a negative probability of being in the state $|1\\rangle$. Clearly this mapping can yield nonsense density matrices. Further, by inspection we can see that the eigenvalues of the resulting density matrix are 1.0625 and -0.0625, meaning not all eigenvalues are positive. Thus the mapping is not \"completely positive\", the \"CP\" in CPTP.\n"
msgstr "En tant que matrice densité physique, cela correspond à une probabilité classique supérieure à 1 que le système soit dans l'état $|0\\rangle$ et à une probabilité négative qu'il soit dans l'état $|1\\rangle$. Cette application peut clairement produire des matrices densité absurdes. De plus, on voit par inspection que les valeurs propres de la matrice densité obtenue sont 1.0625 et -0.0625, ce qui signifie que toutes les valeurs propres ne sont pas positives. L'application n'est donc pas « complètement positive », le « CP » de CPTP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check by explicit calculation that the inverse operation above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ undoes the noise channel and returns the noise-free state.\n"
msgstr "Vérifie par un calcul explicite que l'opération inverse $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ ci-dessus annule le canal de bruit et restitue l'état sans bruit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it to the noisy state:\n"
msgstr "Appliquons-la à l'état bruité :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"This is exactly the original state (up to rounding).\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"C'est exactement l'état d'origine (à l'arrondi près).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We restate to be absolutely clear: we cannot invert the noise channel exactly; the inverse is not CPTP, nor is it a valid physical channel. However, we can effectively invert the channel as a linear combination of physical channels.\n"
msgstr "Nous le répétons pour être absolument clairs : nous ne pouvons pas inverser exactement le canal de bruit ; l'inverse n'est pas CPTP, ni un canal physique valide. Cependant, nous pouvons effectivement inverser le canal sous forme de combinaison linéaire de canaux physiques.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the depolarizing channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"where: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ etc.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour le canal dépolarisant :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"où : $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$, etc.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The inverse can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"L'inverse peut s'écrire :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with:\n"
msgstr "with:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = physically implementable Clifford channels\n"
msgstr "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = canaux de Clifford implémentables physiquement\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probabilities\n"
msgstr "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probabilités\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"
msgstr "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the core idea behind PEC:\n"
msgstr "C'est l'idée centrale de PEC :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample channels according to $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"
msgstr "Échantillonner les canaux selon $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attach signs to measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Attribuer des signes aux résultats de mesure\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values converge to the noise-free value\n"
msgstr "Les valeurs moyennes convergent vers la valeur sans bruit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply PEC \"by hand\" to the estimation of $\\langle Z \\rangle$ by using the density matrix $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ and see if we can recover the results for $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. For $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ we expect:\n"
msgstr "Nous appliquons PEC « à la main » à l'estimation de $\\langle Z \\rangle$ en utilisant la matrice densité $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ et nous voyons si nous pouvons retrouver les résultats de $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. Pour $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$, nous attendons :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that for the noisy density matrix, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Notons aussi que pour la matrice densité bruitée, nous obtenons :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's the right order of magnitude but significantly far from the ideal case.\n"
msgstr "C'est le bon ordre de grandeur, mais très éloigné du cas idéal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we step through how, with the PEC process, we can reconstruct the unbiased expectation value from the noisy density matrix. In real workflows, this is probabilistic and will be automated. In this \"by-hand\" workflow, we will choose probabilistic values that are realistic, but perhaps convenient for our presentation. This should not be taken as a claim that PEC is perfect. This is simply to show you a plausible scenario that could happen inside the PEC packages.\n"
msgstr "Voyons maintenant comment, avec le processus PEC, nous pouvons reconstruire la valeur moyenne non biaisée à partir de la matrice densité bruitée. Dans les workflows réels, cela est probabiliste et automatisé. Dans ce workflow « à la main », nous choisirons des valeurs probabilistes réalistes, mais peut-être commodes pour notre présentation. Cela ne doit pas être interprété comme une affirmation que PEC est parfaite. Il s'agit simplement de te montrer un scénario plausible qui pourrait se produire à l'intérieur des packages PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that our noise channel is of the form:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"The inverse can be written (exactly):\n"
msgstr ""
"Rappelons que notre canal de bruit est de la forme :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"L'inverse peut s'écrire (exactement) :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is simpler for this introduction to focus on the channel's effect on our density matrix. This allows us to work with familiar objects like density matrices and expectation values. To that end, consider what must be true about the effects of this inverse operation on our estimation process: the estimator produced by PEC must be normalized and unbiased. This corresponds to two conditions:\n"
msgstr "Pour cette introduction, il est plus simple de se concentrer sur l'effet du canal sur notre matrice densité. Cela nous permet de travailler avec des objets familiers comme les matrices densité et les valeurs moyennes. Pour cela, considérons ce qui doit être vrai des effets de cette opération inverse sur notre processus d'estimation : l'estimateur produit par PEC doit être normalisé et non biaisé. Cela correspond à deux conditions :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization: To ensure that this operation does not change the scale of the observable, we require that $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. To see why this is the case, we could either consider the action of the inverse on a density matrix, or consider its action on the expectation value of something trivial like $\\mathcal{I}$ itself.\n"
msgstr "Normalisation : pour garantir que cette opération ne change pas l'échelle de l'observable, nous exigeons que $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. Pour comprendre pourquoi, nous pourrions soit considérer l'action de l'inverse sur une matrice densité, soit considérer son action sur la valeur moyenne d'un objet trivial comme $\\mathcal{I}$ lui-même.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibration: In a real workflow, we use calibration circuits to learn noise behavior at a gate level. We then use the gate-level knowledge of noise behavior, and the linearity of expectation values to apply the learned noise model to the larger circuit. In our case, we started with artificial knowledge that the ideal expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. But it would be very easy to come up with a state for which we know theoretically that this would be the ideal value, and then use actual measurements for calibration. A key point is that for PEC, one typically does not learn a full noise model of the entire circuit. Instead, one learns local noise models for individual gates or circuit layers and uses those to construct the quasi-probability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Calibration : dans un workflow réel, nous utilisons des Circuits de calibration pour apprendre le comportement du bruit au niveau des Gates. Nous utilisons ensuite cette connaissance du bruit au niveau des Gates, ainsi que la linéarité des valeurs moyennes, pour appliquer le modèle de bruit appris au Circuit plus grand. Dans notre cas, nous sommes partis de la connaissance artificielle que la valeur moyenne idéale est $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. Mais il serait très facile de trouver un état pour lequel nous savons théoriquement que ce serait la valeur idéale, puis d'utiliser de vraies mesures pour la calibration. Un point clé est que, pour PEC, on n'apprend généralement pas un modèle de bruit complet de tout le Circuit. On apprend plutôt des modèles de bruit locaux pour des Gates ou des couches de Circuit individuelles, et on les utilise pour construire la décomposition en quasi-probabilités.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use these conditions to determine $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. We consider the ansatz\n"
msgstr "Nous utilisons ces conditions pour déterminer $\\alpha$ et $\\beta$. Nous considérons l'ansatz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the Pauli channels act by conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Rappelons que les canaux de Pauli agissent par conjugaison :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ to $\\rho$ gives:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"L'application de $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ à $\\rho$ donne :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taking the trace, we obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"En prenant la trace, nous obtenons :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Pauli operator is unitary, such that conjugation preserves the trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Chaque opérateur de Pauli est unitaire, de sorte que la conjugaison préserve la trace :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the PEC estimator to be normalized, the effective\n"
"inverse map must preserve the trace of all density matrices. That is, we require:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour que l'estimateur PEC soit normalisé, l'application inverse effective\n"
"doit préserver la trace de toutes les matrices densité. C'est-à-dire que nous exigeons :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies the normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cela implique la contrainte de normalisation :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But in our case, this yields the condition:\n"
msgstr "Mais dans notre cas, cela donne la condition :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we use calibration information to relate the observed expectation value to the known ideal one.\n"
msgstr "Nous utilisons maintenant les informations de calibration pour relier la valeur moyenne observée à la valeur idéale connue.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving our two conditions for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "En résolvant nos deux conditions pour $\\alpha$ et $\\beta$, nous obtenons :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These coefficients sum to 1, but one of them is negative.\n"
msgstr "Ces coefficients ont pour somme 1, mais l'un d'eux est négatif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can recover the ideal expectation value by randomly modifying the circuit, measuring, multiplying the result by a signed weight, and averaging. In particular, no density matrices are reconstructed and no inverse channel is implemented physically.\n"
msgstr "Nous pouvons retrouver la valeur moyenne idéale en modifiant aléatoirement le Circuit, en mesurant, en multipliant le résultat par un poids signé, puis en faisant la moyenne. En particulier, aucune matrice densité n'est reconstruite et aucun canal inverse n'est implémenté physiquement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key step: this is PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"
msgstr "L'étape clé : c'est PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For our noise strength $p=0.15$, the inverse channel can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour notre intensité de bruit $p=0.15$, le canal inverse peut s'écrire :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important facts:\n"
msgstr "Faits importants :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The coefficients sum to 1\n"
msgstr "Les coefficients ont pour somme 1\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "One coefficient is negative\n"
msgstr "Un coefficient est négatif\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each term is physically implementable\n"
msgstr "Chaque terme est implémentable physiquement\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The negativity moves into classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "La négativité est reportée dans le post-traitement classique\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We form a sampling distribution from the absolute values of the weights:\n"
msgstr "Nous formons une distribution d'échantillonnage à partir des valeurs absolues des poids :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\alpha| = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"|\\beta| = 0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(for each of X, Y, Z)\n"
msgstr "(pour chacun de X, Y, Z)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Total weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Poids total :\n"
"$$\n"
"W = 1.1875 + 3\\times0.0625 = 1.375\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For sampling probabilities, divide by W.\n"
msgstr "Pour obtenir les probabilités d'échantillonnage, divise par W.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Operation | Probability | Sign |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Do nothing ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Apply X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Apply Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Opération | Probabilité | Signe |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|------|\n"
"| Ne rien faire ($\\mathcal{I}$) |1.1875 / 1.375 ≈ 0.864 |+ |\n"
"| Appliquer X | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Appliquer Y | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"
"| Appliquer Z | 0.0625 / 1.375 ≈ 0.045 | - |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sign comes from the original coefficient, not the probability.\n"
msgstr "Le signe provient du coefficient d'origine, pas de la probabilité.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each shot consists of these steps:\n"
msgstr "Chaque shot se compose des étapes suivantes :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the state\n"
msgstr "Préparer l'état\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the hardware apply the noisy circuit\n"
msgstr "Laisser le matériel appliquer le Circuit bruité\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomly choose an operation from the table above using the associated probabilities\n"
msgstr "Choisir aléatoirement une opération dans le tableau ci-dessus selon les probabilités associées\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it\n"
msgstr "Apply it\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure $Z$, getting $\\pm 1$\n"
msgstr "Mesurer $Z$, ce qui donne $\\pm 1$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the outcome by $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"
msgstr "Multiplier le résultat par $\\text{sign} \\times W$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Record that number\n"
msgstr "Enregistrer ce nombre\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now do examples of several shots.\n"
msgstr "Voyons maintenant des exemples de plusieurs shots.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 1 (identity case)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 1 (cas de l'identité)**\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose our randomly chosen operation is the identity $\\mathcal{I}$ (or equivalently: do nothing). Based on the arguments and the table above, this will happen 86.4% of the time. Because the coefficient of $\\mathcal{I}$ in the inverse of the noise channel is positive, we select the $+$ sign. Our measurement of Z could easily yield either $\\pm 1$. Let us suppose it yields $+1$.\n"
msgstr "Supposons que l'opération choisie aléatoirement soit l'identité $\\mathcal{I}$ (ou, de façon équivalente : ne rien faire). D'après les arguments et le tableau ci-dessus, cela se produit dans 86,4 % des cas. Comme le coefficient de $\\mathcal{I}$ dans l'inverse du canal de bruit est positif, nous sélectionnons le signe $+$. Notre mesure de Z pourrait tout aussi bien donner $\\pm 1$. Supposons qu'elle donne $+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The PEC-corrected contribution from this shot would be:\n"
"$(+1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375$\n"
msgstr ""
"La contribution corrigée par PEC de ce shot serait :\n"
"$(+1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = +1.375$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Shot 2 (identity again)**\n"
msgstr "**Shot 2 (à nouveau l'identité)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose we again obtain $\\mathcal{I}$ as our random operation (so the sign of the term is initially still $+$), but this time our measurement of Z yields $-1$. This time the contribution is:\n"
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Supposons que nous obtenions à nouveau $\\mathcal{I}$ comme opération aléatoire (le signe du terme est donc toujours $+$ au départ), mais que cette fois notre mesure de Z donne $-1$. Cette fois, la contribution est :\n"
"$$\n"
"(-1) \\times (+1) \\times 1.375 = -1.375\n"
"$$\n"

